# dfdreview builds the review page of a leveled design at a stage boundary.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number docs/flow.dfd -o flow.svg

{Agent at a stage boundary}
> options
[1. Open the repository
 to read each file in both versions
 (repo.Open)]
> repository, options
[2. Read the design in both versions
 with its vocabulary
 (design.Read)]
> design, repository
[3. Index the declarations and the changed files
 so each reference finds its code
 (code.Read)]
> design, code index, options
[4. Draw each diagram before, as a diff and after
 with links to code, types and terms
 (draw.Views)]
> views, options
[5. Read the notes
 from the plan, the score cards and the report
 (notes.Read)]
> views, design, code index, notes
[6. Write the page
 (dfdreview.writePage)]
> review page
{Reviewer}

# type: options = dfdreview.Options
# type: repository = *repo.Repo
# type: design = *design.Design
# type: code index = *code.Index
# type: views = []draw.View
# type: notes = *notes.Notes
# type: review page = HTML file
